{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Enumeration","externalID":"s:14ColoringModule0A8StrategyO","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ColoringStrategy","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Coloring.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ColoringModule\/Coloring.swift#L109"},"title":"ColoringStrategy","modules":[{"name":"ColoringModule"}],"symbolKind":"enum","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ColoringStrategy","kind":"identifier"}]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Enumeration Cases","anchor":"Enumeration-Cases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/coloredNeighbors","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/connectedSequentialBreadthFirst","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/connectedSequentialDepthFirst","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/independentSet","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/largestFirst","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/saturationLargestFirst","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/smallestLast"],"generated":true},{"title":"Default Implementations","anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/Equatable-Implementations"],"generated":true}],"abstract":[{"text":"How ","type":"text"},{"code":"greedyColoring(strategy:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" orders the vertices. Each vertex in turn takes the least colour","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"none of its already coloured neighbours has (first fit). Degrees are simple degrees (distinct","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other neighbours, self-loops left out); ties go to the lesser vertex index, except for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":".coloredNeighbors","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/s12CaseIterableP","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/SQ","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/SH","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule"]]},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ColoringStrategy"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://ColoringModule/SH":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/SH","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Hashable"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy/smallestLast":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"ColoringStrategy.smallestLast","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/smallestLast","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/smallestlast","abstract":[{"text":"Matula–Beck: repeatedly remove a vertex of least degree in what is left (the least index on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ties), then colour in the reverse of that removal order. At most degeneracy + 1 colours, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at most 6 on a planar graph. O((n + m) log n).","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"smallestLast","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy","title":"ColoringStrategy","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"How ","type":"text"},{"code":"greedyColoring(strategy:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" orders the vertices. Each vertex in turn takes the least colour","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"none of its already coloured neighbours has (first fit). Degrees are simple degrees (distinct","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other neighbours, self-loops left out); ties go to the lesser vertex index, except for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":".coloredNeighbors","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ColoringStrategy","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ColoringStrategy","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy/Equatable-Implementations":{"url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/equatable-implementations","type":"topic","title":"Equatable Implementations","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/Equatable-Implementations","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy/largestFirst":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Degree descending, the lesser index first on ties: Welsh–Powell, which colours class by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"class in this order and gives the same colouring as first fit. O(n + m)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/largestFirst","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/largestfirst","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"largestFirst","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ColoringStrategy.largestFirst","kind":"symbol"},"doc://ColoringModule/SQ":{"title":"Swift.Equatable","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/SQ","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://ColoringModule/s12CaseIterableP":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.CaseIterable","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/s12CaseIterableP"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy/coloredNeighbors":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"First the vertex of greatest degree (the least index on ties), then repeatedly the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"uncoloured vertex with the most coloured neighbours. Ties among those fall as a two-way"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indexed binary max-heap breaks them, not by index: vertices are pushed in index order and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"raised neighbour by neighbour in ascending order; an entry moves above an equal parent and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sinks to the left child unless the right one is strictly greater. O((n + m) log n)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/coloredNeighbors","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/coloredneighbors","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"coloredNeighbors"}],"title":"ColoringStrategy.coloredNeighbors","kind":"symbol"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy/independentSet":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"ColoringStrategy.independentSet","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/independentSet","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/independentset","abstract":[{"text":"Colour classes one at a time: class k is a maximal independent set of the vertices not yet","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"coloured, built by repeatedly taking the one with the fewest neighbours among those still","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"available (the least index on ties) and making it and its neighbours unavailable.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O(χ (n + m) log n) for χ classes.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"independentSet"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","title":"ColoringModule","type":"topic","abstract":[],"role":"collection"},"doc://ColoringModule/s8SendableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/s8SendableP","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Sendable"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy/connectedSequentialDepthFirst":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The same in depth-first preorder. O(n + m).","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/connectedSequentialDepthFirst","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/connectedsequentialdepthfirst","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"connectedSequentialDepthFirst","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ColoringStrategy.connectedSequentialDepthFirst","kind":"symbol"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy/connectedSequentialBreadthFirst":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/connectedsequentialbreadthfirst","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/connectedSequentialBreadthFirst","title":"ColoringStrategy.connectedSequentialBreadthFirst","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Components by least vertex, each in breadth-first order from its least vertex, neighbours in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order. O(n + m).","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"connectedSequentialBreadthFirst"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/ColoringStrategy/saturationLargestFirst":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy\/saturationlargestfirst","title":"ColoringStrategy.saturationLargestFirst","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/saturationLargestFirst","abstract":[{"text":"DSatur (Brélaz 1979): first a vertex of greatest degree, then repeatedly the uncoloured","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex with the most distinct colours among its neighbours, ties to the greatest degree in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the whole graph, then to the lesser index. Exact on bipartite graphs. O((n + m) log n).","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"saturationLargestFirst"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://ColoringModule/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.SendableMetatype","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"}}}